60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,The candidates are on the table. I am looking for the option that the post-occupancy data suggests will actually be used by the whole campus.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: I am looking for the option that the booking data shows is actually in demand, rather than the one that sits empty.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,I am looking for the option that does not demand more labor from the already exhausted technicians.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,I am looking for the option that avoids the ground-floor hazards and the weather delays that have plagued our recent projects.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I am looking for the option whose costs remain stable in the market, avoiding the twenty percent surge in mechanical plant prices.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, your point about mechanical costs is critical. Does that effectively rule out the laboratory ventilation upgrade?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, yes. The ventilation upgrade is a mechanical plant project, so it absorbs that twenty percent surge directly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I agree. The ventilation upgrade would force our under-staffed technicians to handle complex new systems without any relief.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Toshio, the ventilation upgrade is also a ground-floor project. The survey findings mean hazardous material delays would push it past our weather window.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, exactly. The ventilation upgrade is a mechanical plant project, so it absorbs that twenty percent surge directly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,#### Turn 3 of 4,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: @George, the study commons is the only option that doesn’t add to your technicians’ burden. It’s mostly static infrastructure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Victoria, I appreciate the thought, but a service desk and bookable rooms require front-of-house staff we simply do not have.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the service desk is a single point of contact, not a full-time post. The technicians’ spare hours could cover basic checks, unlike the ventilation system.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, spare hours are not a staffing plan. You are asking for a service desk that the hiring freeze explicitly left unfilled.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, the path network is the only option that avoids the ground-floor hazards and the weather delays you identified.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I object. The path network is entirely exposed to the weather. Your own diaries show six weeks lost to rain and frost.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"@Victoria, I concede the weather risk, but the path network requires no new technical maintenance, unlike the other options.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, I concede the weather risk, but the path network requires no new technical maintenance, unlike the other options.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, the diaries show the loss, but the tender records show surfacing and lamp lots held near the index. The path network avoids the mechanical surge.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
